  "note": "The tokenizer keeps the ASCII apostrophe inside a word and treats U+2019 as a separator, so the same word written both ways produces different tokens. The damage is local to the windows containing the changed character, so length is the variable that matters: a long document still matches on any ten consecutive tokens that contain no apostrophe. This measures verbatim-copy recall when the ONLY change is quote style."
